{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_138","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content scripts/check-repository-artifacts.mjs | Select-Object -First 90'","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env node\r\nimport { execFileSync, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\r\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\r\nimport { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\r\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\r\nimport { parseArgs } from 'node:util';\r\nimport { parseFrontmatter } from '../harness/src/specs.mjs';\r\nimport { isMainEntrypoint } from './lib/entrypoint.mjs';\r\n\r\nconst ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\r\n\r\nexport function isLocalArtifact(path, policy) {\r\n  return policy.localOnlyFiles.includes(path)\r\n    || policy.retiredTests.includes(path)\r\n    || policy.localOnlyDirectories.some((directory) => path === directory || path.startsWith(`${directory}/`))\r\n    || (policy.reviewedDirectories?.some((directory) => path.startsWith(`${directory}/`))\r\n      && !policy.retainedFiles?.includes(path)) === true;\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst IGNORE_START = '# BEGIN reviewed repository inputs (generated by repo:artifacts:check --write-ignore)';\r\nconst IGNORE_END = '# END reviewed repository inputs';\r\n\r\nexport function renderReviewedIgnore(policy) {\r\n  return [IGNORE_START,\r\n    '# New outputs are local by default, including inside an existing acceptance directory.',\r\n    ...(policy.reviewedDirectories ?? []).flatMap((directory) => [\r\n      '/' + directory + '/**', '!/' + directory + '/**/',\r\n    ]),\r\n    ...(policy.retainedFiles ?? []).map((path) => '!/' + path),\r\n    IGNORE_END,\r\n  ].join('\\n');\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport function checkRepositoryArtifacts(root = ROOT) {\r\n  const policy = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(root, 'scripts/repository-artifacts.json'), 'utf8'));\r\n  const tracked = new Set(execFileSync('git', ['ls-files', '-z'], {\r\n    cwd: root,\r\n    encoding: 'utf8',\r\n    maxBuffer: 32 * 1024 * 1024,\r\n    windowsHide: true,\r\n  }).split('\\0').filter(Boolean));\r\n  const issues = [];\r\n  for (const path of tracked) {\r\n    if (isLocalArtifact(path, policy)) issues.push(`Local artifact is still tracked: ${path}`);\r\n  }\r\n  // A tracked path that also matches .gitignore is invisible to ordinary status and\r\n  // would silently travel with every clone. --no-index is deliberately omitted so\r\n  // this covers the exact shadow-tracking class reported by issues #63/#68.\r\n  const shadowTracked = execFileSync('git', ['ls-files', '-i', '-c', '--exclude-standard', '-z'], {\r\n    cwd: root,\r\n    encoding: 'utf8',\r\n    maxBuffer: 32 * 1024 * 1024,\r\n    windowsHide: true,\r\n  }).split('\\0').filter(Boolean);\r\n  for (const path of shadowTracked) issues.push(`Tracked path is ignored: ${path}`);\r\n  const retained = policy.retainedFiles ?? [];\r\n  for (const path of retained) {\r\n    if (path.startsWith('/') || path.includes('..') || /[\\\\*?\\[\\]]/.test(path)\r\n      || !policy.reviewedDirectories?.some((directory) => path.startsWith(directory + '/'))) {\r\n      issues.push('Invalid reviewed input path: ' + path);\r\n    }\r\n    if (!tracked.has(path)) issues.push('Reviewed input is not tracked: ' + path);\r\n    if (!existsSync(join(root, path))) issues.push('Reviewed input is missing: ' + path);\r\n  }\r\n  if (new Set(retained).size !== retained.length) issues.push('Duplicate reviewed input paths');\r\n  if (policy.reviewedDirectories?.length) {\r\n    const ignore = readFileSync(join(root, '.gitignore'), 'utf8').replaceAll('\\r\\n', '\\n');\r\n    const block = ignore.slice(ignore.indexOf(IGNORE_START), ignore.indexOf(IGNORE_END) + IGNORE_END.length);\r\n    if (block !== renderReviewedIgnore(policy)) issues.push('Reviewed ignore rules are stale: run pnpm repo:artifacts:check --write-ignore');\r\n  }\r\n  for (const path of policy.requiredInputs) {\r\n    if (!tracked.has(path)) issues.push(`Required source input is not tracked: ${path}`);\r\n    if (!existsSync(join(root, path))) issues.push(`Required source input is missing: ${path}`);\r\n  }\r\n  for (const path of policy.retiredTests) {\r\n    if (existsSync(join(root, path))) issues.push(`Retired test is still in default discovery: ${path}`);\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const ignored = spawnSync('git', ['check-ignore', '--no-index', '--stdin', '-z'], {\r\n    cwd: root,\r\n    input: `${[...new Set([...policy.requiredInputs, ...retained])].join('\\0')}\\0`,\r\n    encoding: 'utf8',\r\n    windowsHide: true,\r\n  });\r\n  if (ignored.error || ![0, 1].includes(ignored.status)) {\r\n    throw ignored.error ?? new Error(`Cannot inspect ignore rules: ${ignored.stderr}`);\r\n  }\r\n  for (const path of ignored.stdout.split('\\0').filter(Boolean)) {\r\n    issues.push(`Required source input is ignored: ${path}`);\r\n  }\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_140","type":"reasoning","text":"I need to understand how the repository-artifacts.json retainedFiles works and what \"reviewedDirectories\" covers. The harness-gap-closure directory is a reviewedDirectory, and retainedFiles lists specific files inside. New files in that directory (l04-*.md, l04-acceptance.json, L04-SHA256SUMS) would be ignored by .gitignore unless added to retainedFiles. But wait, the L01/L02/L03 files exist in the repo — how are they tracked? Let me check.\n\nActually the retainedFiles listing only includes o01 and baseline and design. But l01, l02, l03 acceptance files are present. Let me look at gitignore to see whether docs/dev/harness-gap-closure is a reviewedDirectory.\n\nHmm, but there's no .git in the agent dir, so git-based checks can't run. But the base dir also has l01-l03 present in docs. Wait — the search I did on ../base showed l01/l02/l03 files. And repository-artifacts.json in the agent dir only lists o01 etc. Let me check base's repository-artifacts.json — maybe the agent dir snapshot is a different state.\n\nActually, let me check whether the l01/l02/l03 files are listed in retainedFiles. My filter for \"*harness-gap*\" returned only those. Let me grep for \"l01-acceptance\".\n\nWait, my filter returned 10 files including ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS, O01-, SHA256SUMS, baseline-*, design.md, o01-*, source-inventory.json. It didn't include l01/l02/l03 or S0x, e01, etc. Hmm, but those files exist. Let me check the reviewedDirectories and whether harness-gap-closure is listed.\n\nActually maybe retainedFiles includes many; my Where-Object filter \"*harness-gap*\" matched only 10. Let me search for \"l01-acceptance\" and \"s01-acceptance\".\n\nLet me grep the json."}}
